Construct terminal biology and virgin per-recruit biomass, and average the
requested historical fishing-pattern years.
@param d Borrowed validated input schema; must outlive the benchmark
calculator.
@param values Borrowed native parameter map, including fixed biology; must
outlive this object.
@param deviations Historical fitted log recruitment deviations, including
early age-structure effects.
@param first_pattern_year First historical year averaged into the fishing
pattern; zero means terminal year.
@param last_pattern_year Last historical year averaged into the fishing
pattern; zero means terminal year.
@details data and values are borrowed; do not destroy or modify them while
using this calculator. Zero reference-year arguments select the terminal
year.

Solve positive Beverton-Holt recruitment, equilibrium abundance, yield and
SS3 units-4 annual F for a nonnegative fishing multiplier.
@param scale Nonnegative common multiplier on the reference apical-rate
pattern.
@return Equilibrium summaries; recruitment is clamped to zero beyond the
positive BH equilibrium.

Use bracket expansion and bisection to find a valid fractional SPR or
virgin-biomass target.
@param value Target fraction in (0,1), interpreted by spawning_ratio.
@param spawning_ratio True targets equilibrium SSB divided by unfished
SSB; false targets raw SPR.
@return Equilibrium summaries at the bracketed target fishing multiplier.

Populate a parameter map from control initial values; these may differ from
fitted Report.sso values.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@param data Parsed controls whose initial native values are read;
report-fitted values are separate fixtures.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Calculate a numerically stable inverse-logit for ordinary or AD scalars.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@param x Unconstrained scalar log-odds; evaluated with a value-based stable
branch.
@return Inverse-logit probability on the same scalar/AD tape as x.

Approximate the standard normal CDF with scalar-generic operations, enabling
differentiation through age-length probabilities.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@param x Standard-normal deviate; derivatives follow the smooth
approximation.
@return Approximate normal cumulative probability on the same scalar/AD tape
as x.

Map a population length-bin lower edge to its integration midpoint,
including the final bin convention.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param bin Zero-based index into the population length integration grid.
@return Integration midpoint in cm.

Locate the start of the subseason containing spawning, matching the supplied
SS3 maturity integration convention.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Build a discrete block-activity cache key for a year; use only within one
evaluation to avoid reusing AD tape vertices.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active
control blocks.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Read one CSV record, accepting LF/CRLF and reporting stream exhaustion.
@param in Input stream; record extraction advances its position.
@param line One unquoted CSV record (or output record buffer for csv_line).
@return True for an extracted record; false only when no next line can be
extracted.

Split the deliberately unquoted, single-line CSV schema; retain empty
fields.
@param line One unquoted CSV record (or output record buffer for csv_line).
@return All fields in order, including a final empty field after a trailing
comma.

Parse an entire decimal integer token; reject suffixes, overflow and blanks.
@param text Entire numeric token; partial parses and coercion are not
accepted.
@return Exactly parsed decimal integer.

Parse an entire finite floating-point token, rejecting range errors and
whitespace.
@param text Entire numeric token; partial parses and coercion are not
accepted.
@return Exactly parsed finite decimal floating-point value.

Construct an explicitly zero-filled sex-by-age state, including AD scalars
whose default constructor does not initialize a numerical zero.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@return A new state containing numerical T(0) in every cell.

Map zero-based sex and age to the flattened 32-cell population-state index;
callers supply sex 0-1 and age 0-15.
@param sex Zero-based sex index: 0 female, 1 male.
@param age Integer model age 0..15, with age 15 representing the plus group.
@return Sex-major offset sex*nage+age; no bounds check is performed by this
primitive.

Assessment calendar, four seasonal durations, spawning month, area count and
plus-group age.
@details first_year/last_year are inclusive calendar years.
seasons/subseasons and plus_age describe the supported discretization;
season_months contains durations, not start months. spawn_month is one-based
calendar timing.

One observed fleet-season catch with year, value and log-scale standard
error; fleet units select tonnes or thousands of fish.
@details value follows the referenced fleet units, while log_se is a
log-scale error. year=-999 carries the supported initialization observation;
normal rows are historical year/season catches, not estimates of apical F.

Propagate a compatible finite output Jacobian through the full parameter
covariance as J V J-transpose, preserving correlations.
@param jacobian Output-by-coordinate derivative matrix, with columns in the
covariance coordinate order.
@param covariance Square, finite, symmetric positive-definite covariance of
independent fitting coordinates.
@return Native output covariance J*V*J-transpose, which may be rank
deficient.
@details Columns of jacobian must correspond exactly to covariance rows.
Keeping only marginal parameter variances would omit compensating/correlated
effects and change the reported uncertainties.

Construct a pointwise positive 95% interval from a positive estimate and
nonnegative native variance; reject nonfinite results.
@param estimate Strictly positive native-scale output estimate.
@param variance Nonnegative finite native-scale marginal variance, not a
standard deviation.
@return Native SE and positive pointwise 95% log-scale Wald bounds.
@details Bounds are estimate*exp(+-1.95996398454005*SE/estimate). They are
not bootstrap quantiles, simultaneous trajectory bands or intervals for
realized future recruitment.

Calculate the stable Baranov exposure (1-exp(-Z*duration))/Z, using a
near-zero expansion; Z is an annual rate and duration is years.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@param z Total annual instantaneous mortality; callers supply nonnegative
rates.
@param duration Exposure duration in calendar years; a quarter is 0.25.
@return Integrated survival per unit abundance; its limit as z tends to zero
is duration.

Advance survivors one age at the calendar-year boundary, retain accumulated
ages in the plus group and clear age zero.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the active
evaluation tape.
@param survivors Post-mortality abundance in thousands of fish, before
January aging.
@return A new January state, retaining old plus-group survivors and
admitting age-14 survivors.

Evaluate the ordinary von Bertalanffy growth curve at a real age using fixed
growth settings and length at birth.
@param real_age Elapsed years since birth, including fractional age.
@param g Fixed growth reference ages, lengths, rate and variability for one
sex.
@param length_at_birth Mean length at birth in cm.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Resolve a component/fleet likelihood lambda at the requested estimation
phase.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param component SS3 likelihood-component code, as stored in lambda_changes.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector
offset.
@param phase Estimation phase used to resolve persistent lambda changes.
@return Effective lambda after applicable changes persist through the
selected phase.

Apply a parsed variance adjustment for an observation kind and fleet to its
initial error value.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param kind SS3 variance-adjustment kind code.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector
offset.
@param initial Default adjustment/error value when no matching control row
exists.
@return Configured replacement value or initial when no row matches.

Resolved season, within-year observation time, age-length-key time and
elapsed seasonal survival duration.
@details season is one-based. time and alk_time are calendar-year fractions;
elapsed is time since the season start. Negative elapsed is an intentional
sentinel for season-integrated sampling, not a negative survival duration.

Translate a source observation month and fleet timing setting into the
season and exposure times used for index and composition prediction.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param fleet One-based source fleet identifier, not a zero-based vector
offset.
@param month Source observation month, in [1,13); fractional months retain
their supplied timing.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Build the fitting-coordinate schema from estimated control parameters and
independent early/main recruitment deviations.
@param input Input schema transferred into the owning model adapter.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param deviations Historical fitted log recruitment deviations, including
early age-structure effects.

Return only the joint scalar objective for a supplied fitting-coordinate
vector.
@tparam T Ordinary or AD scalar; all returned AD values belong to the
active evaluation tape.
@param x Independent bounded-logit coordinates in
free/parameter_names_impl order; length must match free.size().
@return Joint penalized negative log-likelihood; no Laplace or
transform-density term.

Evaluate the piecewise recruitment-bias ramp for a historical year from the
advanced control settings.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active
control blocks.
@return Configured bias-ramp fraction for the year.

Average fitted fleet/season apical rates over checked historical reference
years.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param history Historical trajectory fitted to the original catch series.
@param first First historical reference year, inclusive.
@param last Last historical reference year, inclusive.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Calculate raw per-recruit SPR using that historical year's fishing rates and
selectivity blocks.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param history Historical trajectory fitted to the original catch series.
@param year Calendar year used to select observations, deviations or active
control blocks.
@return Raw SPR, not the report display quantity 1-SPR.

Calculate pooled numbers-weighted annual F over ages 1-10 from January and
end-year abundance, matching SS3 units 4.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param beginning January abundance in thousands of fish before that year
mortality.
@param end December survivors before January aging, on the same scale as
beginning.
@return Pooled annual fishing mortality log(natural-only survivors / actual
survivors) over ages 1..10.

Advance a January state through deterministic future seasons at constant
apical fishing rates, with BH expected recruitment and no future process
deviations.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param january Starting January abundance in thousands of fish; supplied by
value so the caller state is preserved.
@param pattern Fixed fleet/season relative apical fishing-rate pattern for
the projection.
@param scale Nonnegative common multiplier on the reference apical-rate
pattern.
@param years Number of projected calendar years; supported helper range
is 1..200.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.
@details The input January state is copied. No future recruitment errors are
simulated. Annual F is recomputed from transient age weights, so it can vary
even when pattern and scale are fixed.

Write historical annual/seasonal trajectories, fitted indices, length
diagnostics, likelihood components and management reference points to the
supplied output folder. Release publication is performed by the isolated
runner.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param dev Year-to-log-recruitment-deviation map; the caller enforces the
main-period constraint.
@param folder Existing scratch output directory; publication is managed by
the release runner.

Reject unsupported assessment dimensions and changes among 2019-2021
selectivity curves before using a common terminal curve.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.

Recalculate dynamic-baseline, historical-SPR, SPR, MSY and status-quo
targets from a fitted history and solve their fishing multipliers.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param dev Year-to-log-recruitment-deviation map; the caller enforces the
main-period constraint.
@param history Historical trajectory fitted to the original catch series.
@param unfished Counterfactual history with fishing removed and recruitment
feedback recalculated.
@param definitions Five validated scenario rules; each rule is recalibrated
for the supplied parameter values.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.

Rebuild historical state, dynamic baseline, fishing mixture, targets and all
five forecasts for one native parameter/deviation pair.
@param data Validated original-input schema for the supported swordfish
assessment.
@param p Native canonical-name parameter map; all required fixed and
estimated values must be present.
@param dev Year-to-log-recruitment-deviation map; the caller enforces the
main-period constraint.
@param definitions Five validated scenario rules; each rule is recalibrated
for the supplied parameter values.
@return The typed result described above, with the module units and indexing
conventions.
